@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Comment, CommentReport]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/CommentController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/CommentResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/CommentPolicy.ts
+  - db/schema.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/fable-5-1", at: 2026-09-29T16:28:34.276Z }
+---
+
+# Comments hide after three reports
+
+## Context
+
+Readers can comment on posts, and nobody moderates on call. Product
+will not ship comments that one bad actor can fill with spam, so the
+community has to be able to clear a comment off the page by itself. A
+review screen for what was hidden comes later and reads the tables
+directly.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Any signed-in user may comment on any post and report any comment.
+  A comment is deleted by its author or by the author of the post it is
+  on (`CommentPolicy`), and deleting removes the row.
+- `comment_reports` holds one row per report with `(comment_id,
+  user_id)` as its primary key. A repeated report is a no-op
+  (`INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`) and still answers 204.
+- A comment with reports from three or more different users
+  (`REPORTS_TO_HIDE`) is left out of the post page for everyone. The
+  row stays in `comments`.
+- Hidden is **derived on every read** by counting `comment_reports`,
+  not stored as a flag on the comment. Rows the review tooling adds or
+  removes take effect without the app being involved.
+- Comments and their reports are deleted **explicitly**, in one
+  transaction, when a comment or its post is deleted
+  (`Comment.purge`). The schema also declares `ON DELETE CASCADE`, but
+  SQLite skips foreign-key actions unless the connection enabled them,
+  and this app's connection only does after `resetDatabase()`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- One user cannot hide a comment, and cannot inflate the count by
+  reporting again. Three accounts can; rate limiting and sign-up
+  friction are out of scope here.
+- Hidden comments can still be reported and still be deleted by the two
+  people allowed to delete them, including the comment's own author.
+  If review needs hidden comments preserved, deletion has to be refused
+  for them; that is a product decision this ticket did not make.
+- The post page runs one grouped count per view. The threshold changes
+  in one place.
+- Tables written outside the app get `created_at` from a SQL default in
+  the same ISO 8601 text the app writes.
